# Article full texts. The review may read them, it may not redistribute them, so
# no individual article body is carried in Git. What is carried is the inventory,
# the identifiers, and everything the coding derived from the text: the coded
# rows, the extracted items, the verbatim evidence quotes, and the aggregate
# tables. An authorized reviewer restores the texts locally with
# `make fulltext-corpus`, which repeats retrieval and quote verification.
src/05_test_runs/official/01_corpus/fulltext_txt/*
!src/05_test_runs/official/01_corpus/fulltext_txt/.gitkeep

# The API calls behind a run: status, retries, timing, tokens, and cost per call,
# plus the raw call trail. That is bookkeeping about how the run was produced,
# not a coding anyone reads, and it names the exact model versions and spend. It
# stays local; the run manifest and the log go with it.
src/05_test_runs/official/02_model_codings/04_api_calls/
src/05_test_runs/official/02_model_codings/03_by_provider/*/04_api_calls.csv

# The runner's own staging folder. Everything in it is absorbed into the
# published tables and removed, so it only ever exists mid-run.
src/05_test_runs/**/_staging/

# Internal working sections, kept local and never published. 06_data holds the
# retrieval caches and the embedding store; 07_docs the project status write-ups;
# 08_artifacts scratch space for run logs and validation; 09_review_stages the
# stage-by-stage working files of the main pipeline. None of them carries a
# result the team reads: the committed record of a run lives under
# src/05_test_runs.
src/06_data/
src/07_docs/
src/08_artifacts/
src/09_review_stages/
